From 0e5f210b3481a87374e3f6e193a44791673062a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Seyoon Ragavan <complexzetaprime@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 23:53:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Phase-host prefixes through the new last-phase lemmas (gate
 69's major)

Six older proofs rebuilt the tagged-run prefix of a phase host by hand, through
the agreement transfer with the host's table read by unfolding phaseHostTM in
another file: WindowRun's wr_prefix, StepBlock's recordSkipTM_tail, three
haves in Inclusions (b2b_trial_run, b2b_round_run, b2b_finish_answer) and
CodeSimulator's canonEmitVerdict. Each is now an application of
phaseHostTM_run_le with its local guard conversion. OracleSim's
oracleHost_offQuery read the host's table off the redirects the same way; it
is now phaseHostTM_tr_of_red_none. Statements are unchanged; proofs and two
sketches only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
